format: tdxn
version: '2.2'
build: 4
generator: Embody/6.2.72
td_build: 099.2025.32820
network_path: /project1/ferroscope
options:
  include_dat_content: false
  include_storage: true
type_defaults:
  blurTOP:
    parameters:
      extend: mirror
    size: [130, 90]
    color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  constantCHOP:
    parameters:
      autoexportroot: =parent()
      rate: =me.time.rate
    size: [130, 90]
    color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  constantTOP:
    parameters:
      outputresolution: custom
    size: [130, 90]
    color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  feedbackTOP:
    size: [130, 90]
    color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  fitTOP:
    parameters:
      fit: fitoutside
    size: [130, 90]
    color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  flipTOP:
    parameters:
      flipx: =parent.Ferro.par.Mirror
    size: [130, 90]
    color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  glslTOP:
    parameters:
      premultrgbbyalpha: false
    size: [130, 90]
    color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  infoDAT:
    flags:
    - viewer
    size: [130, 90]
    color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  lagCHOP:
    parameters:
      autoexportroot: =parent()
    size: [130, 90]
    color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  nullCHOP:
    parameters:
      autoexportroot: =parent()
    size: [130, 90]
    color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  nullTOP:
    size: [130, 90]
    color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  textDAT:
    parameters:
      extension: frag
      language: glsl
      syncfile: true
    flags:
    - viewer
    size: [130, 90]
    color: [0.9, 0.3, 0.4]
    tags:
    - glsl
type: baseCOMP
custom_pars:
  Presets:
  - name: Preset
    style: Menu
    default: factory
    menuNames:
    - factory
    - mylook
    - blackferro
    - hexhive
    - liquidmarble
    - mirrorface
    - sonobars
    - fractalbloom
    - hexmandala
    menuLabels:
    - Factory Default
    - My Look (2026-10-12)
    - Black Ferrofluid
    - Hex Hive
    - Liquid Marble
    - Mirror Face
    - Sonogram Bars
    - Fractal Bloom
    - Hex Mandala
    help: A saved look. Choose one, then press Apply Preset. Factory Default resets everything (use it when the look is broken); My Look is your tuned state from 2026-10-12. Look presets keep your mic and camera calibration and never change Sources.
    value: fractalbloom
  - name: Applypreset
    style: Pulse
    label: Apply Preset
    help: Copy the chosen preset onto FerroScope. This overwrites the current look.
  - name: Presetname
    style: Str
    label: New Preset Name
    startSection: true
    default: mypreset
    help: Name for Store Current. Letters and digits; an existing name (except Factory Default) is overwritten.
  - name: Storepreset
    style: Pulse
    label: Store Current
    help: Save every current setting (except Sources) as a preset under New Preset Name, and add it to the Preset menu.
  Sources:
  - name: Videosource
    style: Menu
    label: Video Source
    default: camera
    menuNames:
    - camera
    - file
    - external
    - youtube
    menuLabels:
    - Camera
    - Movie File
    - External Input
    - YouTube
    help: 'What drives the viewer pull and the Image page: the webcam, a movie file, any TOP wired into FerroScope''s video input from outside, or the video downloaded from the YouTube Video Link.'
    value: youtube
  - name: Videofile
    style: File
    label: Movie File
    default: $TT/Map/Nature/Movie.1.mp4
    help: Movie (or image) played when Video Source is Movie File.
  - name: Videolink
    style: Str
    label: YouTube Video Link
    startSection: true
    help: A YouTube link (watch, youtu.be or shorts URL) whose picture becomes the video source. Press Download Video to fetch it.
    value: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MtkHmdezGUs
  - name: Videodownload
    style: Pulse
    label: Download Video
    help: Download the YouTube Video Link's picture (H.264, at most 720p, no sound) into media/youtube/ and switch Video Source to YouTube when it is ready. A link downloaded before loads instantly from that folder.
  - name: Videostatus
    style: Str
    label: Video Download
    readOnly: true
    help: Progress of the YouTube video download, the title once it is ready, or why it failed.
    value: 'Ready: Oscar Mulero at Intercell x Yanamaste Invites | ADE 2025'
  - name: Videodownloaded
    style: File
    label: Downloaded Video
    readOnly: true
    help: The downloaded YouTube video file that Video Source YouTube plays (set by Download Video).
    value: media/youtube/MtkHmdezGUs.video.mp4
  - name: Audiosource
    style: Menu
    label: Audio Source
    startSection: true
    default: mic
    menuNames:
    - mic
    - file
    - external
    - youtube
    menuLabels:
    - Microphone
    - Audio File
    - External Input
    - YouTube
    help: 'What feeds the sonogram: the microphone, an audio file, any CHOP wired into FerroScope''s audio input from outside, or the audio downloaded from the YouTube Audio Link (heard through Play to Speakers).'
    value: youtube
  - name: Audiofile
    style: File
    label: Audio File
    default: $TT/Audio/JeremyCaulfield_www.dumb-unit.com.mp3
    help: Audio file played when Audio Source is Audio File.
  - name: Audiolink
    style: Str
    label: YouTube Audio Link
    startSection: true
    help: A YouTube link whose sound feeds the sonogram and the speakers. Leave it empty to use the YouTube Video Link, so one clip gives both picture and sound. Press Download Audio to fetch it.
    value: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MtkHmdezGUs
  - name: Audiodownload
    style: Pulse
    label: Download Audio
    help: Download the audio of the YouTube Audio Link (or of the video link when that is empty) into media/youtube/ and switch Audio Source to YouTube when it is ready. A link downloaded before loads instantly from that folder.
  - name: Audiostatus
    style: Str
    label: Audio Download
    readOnly: true
    help: Progress of the YouTube audio download, the title once it is ready, or why it failed.
    value: 'Ready: Oscar Mulero at Intercell x Yanamaste Invites | ADE 2025'
  - name: Audiodownloaded
    style: File
    label: Downloaded Audio
    readOnly: true
    help: The downloaded YouTube audio file that Audio Source YouTube plays (set by Download Audio).
    value: media/youtube/MtkHmdezGUs.audio.m4a
  - name: Monitor
    style: Toggle
    label: Play to Speakers
    startSection: true
    default: true
    help: Play the file, YouTube or external audio through the default audio device. Never plays the microphone, to avoid feedback.
  - name: Monitorvolume
    style: Float
    label: Speaker Volume
    default: 0.8
    max: 2.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: Volume of the audio played to the speakers.
    value: 0.934
  Transport:
  - name: Link
    style: Menu
    label: Link Audio to Video
    default: auto
    menuNames:
    - auto
    - linked
    - separate
    menuLabels:
    - Auto (Same Clip)
    - Always
    - Never
    help: Whether the audio playhead moves with the video playhead. Auto links them while Video Source and Audio Source play the same clip (one YouTube video, or one file). Always links any file or YouTube video with any file or YouTube audio (past the end of shorter audio the video plays on alone); Never keeps them independent. Live sources (camera, microphone, external input) never link.
  - name: Linked
    style: Toggle
    label: Audio Linked
    readOnly: true
    help: On while the audio follows the video playhead, as decided by Link Audio to Video. Read only.
  - name: Videoplay
    style: Toggle
    label: Play Video
    startSection: true
    default: true
    help: Plays or pauses the movie file or YouTube video. While the audio is linked it plays and pauses the audio too.
  - name: Videotime
    style: Float
    label: Video Position
    clampMin: true
    normMax: 3626.0
    help: Playhead of the movie file or YouTube video in seconds; drag to scrub, or type a time. The slider spans the whole clip. While the audio is linked the audio jumps with it.
  - name: Videoclock
    style: Str
    label: Video Time
    readOnly: true
    help: Video Position and the length of the clip as minutes:seconds (hours:minutes:seconds for clips over an hour). Read only.
  - name: Videospeed
    style: Float
    label: Video Speed
    default: 1
    min: -4.0
    max: 4.0
    normMax: 2.0
    help: 'Playback speed of the movie file or YouTube video: 1 = normal, negative plays backwards. While the audio is linked it sets the audio speed (and pitch) too; linked audio is silent while the video plays backwards.'
  - name: Videoloop
    style: Toggle
    label: Loop Video
    default: true
    help: Loops the video at its end (and at its start when playing backwards); off holds the last frame. While the audio is linked it loops the audio too.
    value: false
  - name: Videorestart
    style: Pulse
    label: Restart Video
    help: Jump the video back to the start. While the audio is linked the audio jumps with it.
  - name: Audioplay
    style: Toggle
    label: Play Audio
    startSection: true
    default: true
    help: Plays or pauses the audio file or YouTube audio. While the audio is linked it plays and pauses the video too.
  - name: Audiotime
    style: Float
    label: Audio Position
    clampMin: true
    normMax: 3626.0
    help: Playhead of the audio file or YouTube audio in seconds; drag to scrub, or type a time. The slider spans the whole file. While the audio is linked the video jumps with it.
  - name: Audioclock
    style: Str
    label: Audio Time
    readOnly: true
    help: Audio Position and the length of the audio as minutes:seconds (hours:minutes:seconds for files over an hour). Read only.
  - name: Audioloop
    style: Toggle
    label: Loop Audio
    default: true
    help: Loops the audio at its end; off stops it there. While the audio is linked it loops the video too.
    value: false
  - name: Audiorestart
    style: Pulse
    label: Restart Audio
    help: Jump the audio back to the start. While the audio is linked the video jumps with it.
  Sound:
  - name: Audioactive
    style: Toggle
    label: Microphone On
    default: true
    help: Turns the microphone input on or off. Off freezes the sonogram on its last state.
    value: false
  - name: Autogain
    style: Toggle
    label: Auto Gain
    startSection: true
    default: true
    help: Follow the loudest frequency band so loud and quiet music both fill the fluid. Off uses the manual Gain.
  - name: Silence
    style: Float
    label: Silence Level (dB)
    default: -42
    min: -90.0
    max: 0.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMin: -70.0
    normMax: -20.0
    help: Auto Gain never treats anything quieter than this as loud, so an empty room stays dark. Raise it if room noise lights the fluid.
    value: -20.9
  - name: Recovery
    style: Float
    label: Gain Recovery (dB/s)
    default: 6
    min: 0.1
    max: 60.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMin: 1.0
    normMax: 20.0
    help: How fast Auto Gain turns back up after a loud moment, in decibels per second.
    value: 20
  - name: Gain
    style: Float
    label: Gain (dB)
    default: 20
    min: -40.0
    max: 100.0
    normMax: 80.0
    help: Manual input gain in decibels, used when Auto Gain is off. Raise it until quiet sound lights the spikes.
    value: 80
  - name: Range
    style: Float
    label: Dynamic Range (dB)
    default: 36
    min: 6.0
    max: 120.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMin: 12.0
    normMax: 90.0
    help: Decibel range below the loudest band (Auto Gain) or below 0 dB (manual) that is shown. Smaller values make quiet bands go dark sooner.
    value: 90
  - name: Tilt
    style: Float
    label: Treble Tilt (dB)
    default: 6
    min: -24.0
    max: 48.0
    normMin: -12.0
    normMax: 36.0
    help: Extra gain added gradually from the lowest to the highest frequency shown, in decibels. Positive values lift the treble, which is usually much quieter than the bass.
    value: -12
  - name: Attack
    style: Float
    label: Attack (s)
    startSection: true
    default: 0.03
    max: 2.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 0.5
    help: How quickly a frequency band rises when it gets louder, in seconds.
    value: 0
  - name: Release
    style: Float
    label: Release (s)
    default: 0.35
    max: 5.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 2.0
    help: How slowly a frequency band falls back when it gets quieter, in seconds. Longer values make the fluid more viscous.
    value: 1.22
  - name: Resetsono
    style: Pulse
    label: Clear Sonogram
    startSection: true
    help: Erases the sonogram history.
  Sonogram:
  - name: Fftsize
    style: Menu
    label: FFT Size
    default: '4096'
    menuNames:
    - '1024'
    - '2048'
    - '4096'
    - '8192'
    - '16384'
    menuLabels:
    - 1024 (fast, coarse bass)
    - '2048'
    - '4096'
    - 8192 (fine bass)
    - 16384 (finest, slowest)
    help: Analysis window of the spectrum. Larger = finer bass detail (less blocky low end) but a slower reaction.
    value: '1024'
  - name: Logscale
    style: Float
    label: Log Frequency Scale
    default: 1
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: 1 = every octave gets the same width (musical, bass spread out). 0 = linear Hz (treble takes most of the width).
    value: 0.904
  - name: Specstart
    style: Float
    label: Spectrum Start
    startSection: true
    default: 0.18
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: Where the shown frequency range starts on the logarithmic spectrum, 0 = lowest frequency. Raise it to drop rumble.
    value: 1
  - name: Specend
    style: Float
    label: Spectrum End
    default: 0.92
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: Where the shown frequency range ends on the logarithmic spectrum, 1 = highest frequency. Lower it to drop the near-silent top octave.
    value: 0.175
  - name: Freqsmooth
    style: Float
    label: Frequency Smoothing
    max: 16.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 8.0
    help: Blur across neighbouring frequencies, in bins. Removes blocky steps in the bass.
  - name: Bands
    style: Int
    max: 128.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 64.0
    help: Split the spectrum into this many flat bands, like a bar graph. 0 = continuous.
  - name: Freqlayout
    style: Menu
    label: Frequency Layout
    default: lowhigh
    menuNames:
    - lowhigh
    - highlow
    - basscenter
    - treblecenter
    menuLabels:
    - Low to High
    - High to Low
    - Mirrored, Bass in the Middle
    - Mirrored, Treble in the Middle
    help: How frequencies are laid out across the sonogram (and across each kaleidoscope wedge).
    value: treblecenter
  - name: Scrollspeed
    style: Float
    label: Scroll Speed
    startSection: true
    default: 1
    min: 0.1
    max: 6.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMin: 0.25
    normMax: 4.0
    help: How many sonogram rows scroll down per frame (top = newest sound). 1 shows about 4 seconds of history; fractional values scroll on some frames only.
    value: 0.25
  - name: Timeflow
    style: Menu
    label: Time Flow
    default: forward
    menuNames:
    - forward
    - reverse
    - centerout
    - edgesin
    menuLabels:
    - Forward
    - Reverse
    - From the Middle Outward
    - From the Edges Inward
    help: 'Where the newest sound appears and which way it flows: Forward = top to bottom (rim to centre in Radial and tile modes).'
    value: centerout
  - name: Sonogamma
    style: Float
    label: Loudness Contrast
    startSection: true
    default: 1
    min: 0.2
    max: 4.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMin: 0.3
    normMax: 3.0
    help: Gamma on loudness. Above 1 only loud sounds stand out; below 1 quiet sounds show more.
    value: 2.02
  - name: Onsetboost
    style: Float
    label: Onset Punch
    max: 3.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 2.0
    help: Extra height for sudden attacks such as drums and plosives.
  Color:
  - name: Basscolor
    style: RGBA
    label: Bass Color
    size: 3
    default: [0.1, 0.2, 1]
    help: Colour of the lowest frequencies.
    values: [1, 0, 0.552941]
  - name: Lowmidcolor
    style: RGBA
    label: Low-Mid Color
    size: 3
    default: [0.9, 0.08, 0.62]
    help: Colour of the lower middle frequencies (voice fundamentals).
    values: [0.956863, 1, 0.498039]
  - name: Highmidcolor
    style: RGBA
    label: High-Mid Color
    size: 3
    default: [1, 0.52, 0.06]
    help: Colour of the upper middle frequencies (voice clarity, snares).
    values: [1, 0.498039, 0.501961]
  - name: Treblecolor
    style: RGBA
    label: Treble Color
    size: 3
    default: [0.45, 0.95, 1]
    help: Colour of the highest frequencies (hiss, cymbals, sibilants).
  - name: Quietcolor
    style: RGBA
    label: Quiet Color
    size: 3
    startSection: true
    default: [0.006, 0.008, 0.014]
    help: Colour of the fluid where a frequency is silent. Near black keeps the classic ferrofluid look.
  - name: Peakcolor
    style: RGBA
    label: Peak Color
    size: 3
    default: [1, 0.95, 0.86]
    help: Colour the loudest frequencies blend toward above the Peak Threshold.
    values: [10, 10, 0]
  - name: Colorcurve
    style: Float
    label: Amplitude Curve
    startSection: true
    default: 0.8
    min: 0.1
    max: 5.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMin: 0.25
    normMax: 3.0
    help: Gamma from loudness to colour. Below 1 colours quiet sounds early; above 1 keeps colour for loud sounds only.
    value: 0.25
  - name: Peakthreshold
    style: Float
    label: Peak Threshold
    default: 0.7
    min: 0.05
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: Loudness (0-1) at which a frequency reaches its full colour; above it the colour heads toward Peak Color.
    value: 0.05
  - name: Peakmix
    style: Float
    label: Peak Mix
    default: 0.55
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: How far the loudest sounds blend into Peak Color. 0 keeps pure frequency colours.
    value: 0.699
  Fluid:
  - name: Gridshape
    style: Menu
    label: Grid
    default: hex
    menuNames:
    - hex
    - square
    menuLabels:
    - Hexagonal
    - Square
    help: Lattice the spikes stand on. Hexagonal matches real ferrofluid and the 6-segment kaleidoscope.
  - name: Gridcells
    style: Float
    label: Grid Cells
    default: 44
    min: 6.0
    max: 160.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMin: 12.0
    normMax: 100.0
    help: Number of spikes across the width of the image.
    value: 12
  - name: Gridrotate
    style: Float
    label: Grid Rotation
    min: -180.0
    max: 180.0
    help: Rotation of the spike lattice, in degrees.
    value: 0.307
  - name: Cellrandom
    style: Float
    label: Cell Randomness
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: Random offset of every spike from the perfect lattice, for a more organic surface.
    value: 0.813
  - name: Gridamount
    style: Float
    label: Grid Amount
    default: 0.85
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: 0 = a continuous liquid relief of the sonogram, 1 = separate spikes on a thin pool.
    value: 0.253
  - name: Structure
    style: Menu
    startSection: true
    default: spikes
    menuNames:
    - spikes
    - honeycomb
    - both
    menuLabels:
    - Spikes
    - Honeycomb Ridges
    - Spikes + Honeycomb
    help: Spikes at the cell centres, raised honeycomb ridges along the cell edges, or both.
    value: honeycomb
  - name: Ridgewidth
    style: Float
    label: Ridge Width
    default: 0.15
    min: 0.01
    max: 0.5
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: Width of the honeycomb ridges, relative to the cell size.
    value: 0.5
  - name: Spikeshape
    style: Menu
    label: Spike Shape
    startSection: true
    default: cone
    menuNames:
    - cone
    - hexpyramid
    - dome
    - ring
    menuLabels:
    - Cone
    - Hexagonal Pyramid
    - Dome
    - Ring (Crater)
    help: Cone (classic ferrofluid), faceted hexagonal pyramid, rounded dome, or a ring-shaped crater.
  - name: Spikewidth
    style: Float
    label: Spike Width
    default: 0.6
    min: 0.2
    max: 2.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: Spike base width relative to the grid spacing. Above about 0.9 neighbouring spikes merge.
    value: 0.2
  - name: Sharpness
    style: Float
    label: Spike Sharpness
    default: 2.5
    min: 0.5
    max: 6.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: 'Profile of each spike: 1 = straight cone, higher = needle tips with concave flanks.'
    value: 0.5
  - name: Height
    style: Float
    label: Spike Height
    default: 1
    max: 4.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 2.5
    help: Overall height of the spikes and the pool.
    value: 2.5
  - name: Tension
    style: Float
    label: Surface Tension
    default: 0.06
    min: 0.002
    max: 0.5
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMin: 0.002
    normMax: 0.3
    help: How much neighbouring spikes melt together at their bases.
    value: 0.3
  - name: Subgrid
    style: Float
    label: Sub-Grid
    startSection: true
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: Height of a finer lattice of small spikes nested between the large ones.
    value: 0.982
  - name: Subgridscale
    style: Float
    label: Sub-Grid Density
    default: 3
    min: 1.5
    max: 6.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: How much finer the nested lattice is than the main one.
    value: 1.5
  - name: Idle
    style: Float
    label: Idle Level
    startSection: true
    default: 0.3
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: Minimum spike height that keeps breathing when the room is silent, so the fluid never stops moving.
    value: 0.247
  - name: Viscosity
    style: Float
    max: 0.95
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: 'Inertia of the liquid: spikes rise and fall sluggishly. 0 = instant.'
  - name: Ripples
    style: Float
    startSection: true
    max: 2.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: Rings rippling across the pool from the kaleidoscope centre, stronger when loud.
  - name: Ripplefreq
    style: Float
    label: Ripple Density
    default: 8
    min: 1.0
    max: 40.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMin: 2.0
    normMax: 20.0
    help: Number of ripple rings per unit of distance.
    value: 2.1
  Warp:
  - name: Warptype
    style: Menu
    label: Warp Type
    default: noise
    menuNames:
    - noise
    - curl
    - ripple
    - 'off'
    menuLabels:
    - Noise Flow
    - Curl Streams
    - Radial Ripple
    - 'Off'
    help: 'How the liquid surface is twisted: flowing noise, curl streams (swirling currents), radial ripples from the centre, or off.'
    value: ripple
  - name: Wobble
    style: Float
    label: Liquid Wobble
    default: 1
    max: 4.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 2.0
    help: How far the liquid surface and spike positions sway.
    value: 0.46
  - name: Warpscale
    style: Float
    label: Warp Scale
    default: 1
    min: 0.1
    max: 6.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMin: 0.2
    normMax: 4.0
    help: 'Size of the eddies: higher = smaller, busier twists.'
    value: 3.59
  - name: Warpdetail
    style: Int
    label: Warp Detail
    default: 2
    min: 1.0
    max: 4.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: 'Octaves of warp detail: 1 = smooth, 4 = finely crinkled.'
    value: 1
  - name: Flowspeed
    style: Float
    label: Liquid Speed
    startSection: true
    default: 0.35
    max: 4.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 1.5
    help: Speed of the liquid sway.
    value: 0.75
  - name: Agitation
    style: Float
    label: Sound Agitation
    default: 2
    max: 10.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 5.0
    help: How much overall loudness speeds up the liquid sway.
    value: 3.92
  - name: Swirl
    style: Float
    startSection: true
    min: -720.0
    max: 720.0
    normMin: -360.0
    normMax: 360.0
    help: 'Vortex around the kaleidoscope centre: rotation at the centre in degrees, fading outward.'
    value: -360
  - name: Swirlradius
    style: Float
    label: Swirl Radius
    default: 0.4
    min: 0.05
    max: 2.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: How far the vortex reaches from the centre.
    value: 0.169
  Kaleido:
  - name: Kaleidomode
    style: Menu
    label: Kaleidoscope
    default: radial
    menuNames:
    - 'off'
    - mirror
    - radial
    - triangle
    - square
    - hexcells
    - fractal
    - spiral
    menuLabels:
    - 'Off'
    - Mirror Wedges
    - Radial
    - Triangle (3 mirrors, hex tiling)
    - Square Tiles
    - Hex Cells
    - Fractal Fold
    - Log Spiral
    help: 'Off: the plain sonogram. Mirror: mirror wedges over the sonogram. Radial: frequency across each wedge, time along the radius. Triangle: a three-mirror kaleidoscope tiling the plane with hexagons. Square: a four-mirror tiling. Hex Cells: a six-fold mandala in every hexagon. Fractal: repeated folding. Spiral: an endless logarithmic spiral.'
    value: hexcells
  - name: Segments
    style: Int
    default: 6
    min: 1.0
    max: 24.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMin: 1.0
    normMax: 12.0
    help: Number of mirrored wedge pairs around the centre. 6 matches the hexagonal grid.
    value: 11
  - name: Zoom
    style: Float
    default: 0.7
    min: 0.05
    max: 4.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMin: 0.2
    normMax: 2.0
    help: Size of the sonogram inside the kaleidoscope. In Radial mode this is the radius where the newest sound appears.
    value: 0.2
  - name: Zoompulse
    style: Float
    label: Zoom Pulse
    max: 3.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: Zoom pumps with the loudness.
  - name: Center
    style: XYZW
    label: Centre Offset
    size: 2
    min: -1.0
    help: Offset of the kaleidoscope centre from the middle of the screen (added to Follow on the Viewer page).
  - name: Spin
    style: Float
    label: Spin (deg/s)
    startSection: true
    default: 3
    min: -90.0
    max: 90.0
    normMin: -20.0
    normMax: 20.0
    help: Rotation speed of the kaleidoscope, in degrees per second.
    value: -0.2
  - name: Spinreact
    style: Float
    label: Spin Reactivity
    max: 5.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 3.0
    help: Loud sound spins the kaleidoscope faster.
  - name: Sway
    style: Float
    label: Sway (deg)
    max: 180.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 60.0
    help: Back-and-forth rotation amplitude, in degrees.
    value: 18.8
  - name: Swayspeed
    style: Float
    label: Sway Speed (Hz)
    default: 0.15
    max: 3.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: Back-and-forth rotations per second.
    value: 0.771
  - name: Twist
    style: Float
    default: 0.8
    min: -10.0
    max: 10.0
    normMin: -3.0
    normMax: 3.0
    help: 'Spiral twist: extra rotation in radians per unit of distance from the centre.'
    value: -0.36
  - name: Pinch
    style: Float
    label: Radial Pinch
    default: 1
    min: 0.3
    max: 3.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: Below 1 bulges the centre outward like a fisheye, above 1 pulls it in.
    value: 0.3
  - name: Rings
    style: Float
    startSection: true
    max: 30.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 12.0
    help: Split the kaleidoscope into concentric rings that rotate against each other. 0 = off.
    value: 11.93
  - name: Ringspin
    style: Float
    label: Ring Spin (deg/s)
    default: 20
    min: -180.0
    max: 180.0
    normMin: -60.0
    normMax: 60.0
    help: Speed of the counter-rotating rings, in degrees per second.
    value: -2.2
  - name: Tilesize
    style: Float
    label: Tile Size
    startSection: true
    default: 0.35
    min: 0.05
    max: 2.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMin: 0.1
    help: Size of one tile in the Triangle, Square and Hex Cells modes.
    value: 0.1
  - name: Tileoffset
    style: Float
    label: Tile Time Offset
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: Each tile shows a different moment of the sonogram instead of all the same.
    value: 0.048
  - name: Iterations
    style: Int
    label: Fold Iterations
    startSection: true
    default: 4
    min: 1.0
    max: 10.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: 'Fractal mode: number of folds. More = more intricate.'
    value: 1
  - name: Foldscale
    style: Float
    label: Fold Scale
    default: 1.6
    min: 1.0
    max: 3.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: 'Fractal mode: scale applied at each fold.'
    value: 1
  - name: Foldangle
    style: Float
    label: Fold Angle
    default: 30
    min: -180.0
    max: 180.0
    help: 'Fractal mode: rotation at each fold, in degrees.'
    value: 0.892
  - name: Foldoffset
    style: Float
    label: Fold Offset
    default: 0.3
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: 'Fractal mode: shift at each fold; changes the motif.'
    value: 0.506
  Viewer:
  - name: Videoactive
    style: Toggle
    label: Camera On
    default: true
    help: Turns the webcam on or off. Off releases the viewer pull.
  - name: Mirror
    style: Toggle
    label: Mirror Camera
    default: true
    help: Mirror the camera so moving your right hand pulls the right side of the image.
  - name: Pull
    style: Float
    startSection: true
    default: 1.4
    max: 5.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 3.0
    help: 'How strongly the viewer pulls the fluid: spikes rise and lean toward where you are.'
    value: 1.8099999428
  - name: Lens
    style: Float
    default: 1
    max: 4.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 2.0
    help: How much the fluid bulges and magnifies toward the viewer, as if coming out of the screen.
    value: 2
  - name: Follow
    style: Float
    default: 0.6
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: How far the kaleidoscope centre moves toward the viewer, so the fluid streams toward you.
    value: 0.627
  - name: Proximityzoom
    style: Float
    label: Proximity Zoom
    default: 0.8
    max: 4.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 2.0
    help: How much the fluid grows toward you as you come closer to the camera.
    value: 0.69
  - name: Proximityrange
    style: Float
    label: Proximity Range
    default: 0.35
    min: 0.05
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: Share of the camera image you must fill to count as fully close. Lower values reach full proximity from further away.
    value: 0.717
  - name: Sensitivity
    style: Float
    startSection: true
    default: 0.5
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: How different from the empty room a pixel must be to count as you. Raise it in a dim room or with a plain background.
    value: 0.4280000031
  - name: Presenceweight
    style: Float
    label: Presence Weight
    default: 1
    max: 2.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: Strength of your body (difference from the learned empty room) in the pull field.
    value: 0.711
  - name: Motionweight
    style: Float
    label: Motion Weight
    default: 1
    max: 2.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: Strength of movement (frame-to-frame change) in the pull field, so moving hands pull hardest.
    value: 0.5479999781
  - name: Relearnbg
    style: Pulse
    label: Relearn Background
    startSection: true
    help: 'Step out of the frame and press: the current image becomes the empty room. The background also re-learns slowly by itself.'
  Image:
  - name: Imgvisible
    style: Float
    label: Image Visibility
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: How much the camera picture colours the fluid. 0 = sound colours only, 1 = the camera colours.
    value: 1
  - name: Imgrelief
    style: Float
    label: Image Relief
    max: 3.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 1.5
    help: 'How far the camera picture protrudes from the fluid: bright parts rise out of the surface.'
  - name: Imgspikes
    style: Float
    label: Image Spikes
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: How much the camera picture sets the spike heights. At 1 the spikes draw the picture like a halftone.
    value: 1
  - name: Imgsource
    style: Menu
    label: Image Source
    startSection: true
    default: full
    menuNames:
    - full
    - viewer
    - silhouette
    - edges
    menuLabels:
    - Full Image
    - Viewer Only
    - Silhouette
    - Edges
    help: 'Full Image: the whole camera frame. Viewer Only: the picture only where the viewer is. Silhouette: the viewer as a flat shape. Edges: outlines.'
    value: silhouette
  - name: Imggain
    style: Float
    label: Image Gain
    default: 1
    max: 8.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 4.0
    help: Brightens the camera picture before contrast. Raise it in a dim room.
    value: 4
  - name: Imgcontrast
    style: Float
    label: Image Contrast
    default: 1
    max: 5.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 3.0
    help: Contrast of the picture before it shapes the fluid.
    value: 0
  - name: Imginvert
    style: Toggle
    label: Invert Image
    help: Dark parts of the picture rise instead of bright parts.
  - name: Imgsoft
    style: Float
    label: Image Softness (px)
    default: 2
    max: 30.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 15.0
    help: Blur of the camera picture, in pixels. Softer = smoother relief.
    value: 14.91
  - name: Imgkaleido
    style: Toggle
    label: Image Through Kaleidoscope
    help: Mirror the camera picture with the kaleidoscope wedges too, instead of keeping it where you are.
  Look:
  - name: Relief
    style: Float
    default: 0.9
    max: 4.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 2.5
    help: Visual steepness of the spikes in the lighting. Higher = sharper, more three-dimensional spikes.
    value: 2.5
  - name: Gloss
    style: Float
    default: 80
    min: 2.0
    max: 400.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMin: 8.0
    normMax: 200.0
    help: Sharpness of the specular highlights. Ferrofluid is a near-mirror, so this sits high.
    value: 195
  - name: Reflection
    style: Float
    default: 1
    max: 4.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 3.0
    help: Strength of the environment reflections on the spike flanks.
    value: 0
  - name: Rim
    style: Float
    label: Sound Color Rim
    default: 1.5
    max: 6.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 4.0
    help: Brightness of the sound colours reflected on the spike flanks.
    value: 3.86
  - name: Bodycolor
    style: Float
    label: Body Color
    default: 0.15
    max: 3.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 2.0
    help: How much of the sound colour shows in the body of the fluid. 0 = black ferrofluid, colour only in reflections.
    value: 2
  - name: Glow
    style: Float
    label: Tip Glow
    default: 0.3
    max: 5.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 3.0
    help: Emissive glow of the tall, loud spike tips in their sound colour.
    value: 0.99
  - name: Sonoglow
    style: Float
    label: Sonogram Glow
    max: 3.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 1.5
    help: Glow of the sonogram colours across the whole surface, independent of spike height.
    value: 1.5
  - name: Keylight
    style: Float
    label: Key Light
    startSection: true
    default: 1
    max: 5.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 3.0
    help: Brightness of the white softbox highlight on the spikes.
    value: 1.61
  - name: Keycolor
    style: RGBA
    label: Key Color
    size: 3
    default: [1, 0.96, 0.9]
    help: Colour of the softbox highlight.
    values: [1, 1, 1]
  - name: Lightfollow
    style: Float
    label: Light Follows Viewer
    default: 0.4
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: How far the key light swings toward the viewer, so highlights track you.
    value: 0.994
  - name: Bloom
    style: Float
    startSection: true
    default: 0.6
    max: 4.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 2.0
    help: Glow around the brightest highlights.
    value: 1.93
  - name: Exposure
    style: Float
    min: -6.0
    max: 6.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMin: -3.0
    normMax: 3.0
    help: Overall exposure in stops before tone mapping.
    value: 2.93
  - name: Debugview
    style: Menu
    label: Debug View
    startSection: true
    default: 'off'
    menuNames:
    - 'off'
    - field
    - sonogram
    - height
    menuLabels:
    - 'Off'
    - Viewer Field
    - Sonogram
    - Height Field
    help: 'Overlay an internal stage to tune it: the viewer pull field, the raw sonogram, or the height field.'
  - name: Openwindow
    style: Pulse
    label: Open Output Window
    startSection: true
    help: Open the output in its own window (1280 x 720). Esc over the window closes it.
  - name: Closewindow
    style: Pulse
    label: Close Output Window
    help: Close the output window.
parameters:
  parentshortcut: Ferro
flags:
- viewer
color: [0.3, 0.5, 0.9]
tags:
- tdxn
- tdxn_exclude:Audioclock
- tdxn_exclude:Audiotime
- tdxn_exclude:Linked
- tdxn_exclude:Videoclock
- tdxn_exclude:Videotime
comment: Mic sonogram -> kaleidoscopic ferrofluid; webcam presence pulls the fluid toward the viewer.
storage:
  _t_dl_before:
    $type: tuple
    $value:
    - 'Ready: Oscar Mulero at Intercell x Yanamaste Invites | ADE 2025'
    - 1414.6
operators:
- name: CRT
  type: baseCOMP
  parameters:
    parentshortcut: CRT
  position: [5600, 0]
  size: [160, 130]
  color: [0.3, 0.5, 0.9]
  comment: 'Reusable CRT filter: TOP in -> analog signal + tube emulation -> TOP out. Portable copy: components/CRT.tox'
  tags:
  - tdxn
  inputs:
  - tonemap_out
  tdn_ref: project1/ferroscope/CRT.tdxn
- name: out1
  type: outTOP
  parameters:
    label: =me.name
  flags:
  - display
  position: [6400, 0]
  size: [130, 90]
  color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  inputs:
  - null_final
- name: fit_cam
  type: fitTOP
  parameters:
    resolutionw: 160
    resolutionh: 90
  position: [400, -2000]
  inputs:
  - null_video
- name: fit_img
  type: fitTOP
  parameters:
    resolutionw: 640
    resolutionh: 360
  position: [400, -2800]
  inputs:
  - null_video
- name: presets
  type: tableDAT
  parameters:
    file: project1/ferroscope/presets.tsv
    syncfile: true
    rows: 122
    cols: 10
  position: [5600, -400]
  size: [130, 90]
  color: [0.9, 0.3, 0.4]
  tags:
  - tsv
- name: blur_img
  type: blurTOP
  parameters:
    size: =parent.Ferro.par.Imgsoft
  position: [1200, -2800]
  inputs:
  - flip_img
- name: flip_cam
  type: flipTOP
  position: [800, -2000]
  inputs:
  - fit_cam
- name: flip_img
  type: flipTOP
  position: [800, -2800]
  inputs:
  - fit_img
- name: in_audio
  type: inCHOP
  parameters:
    label: =me.name
    connectorder: 1
    autoexportroot: =parent()
  position: [-1600, 200]
  size: [130, 90]
  color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  inputs:
  - const_silence
- name: in_video
  type: inTOP
  parameters:
    label: =me.name
  position: [-1600, -2400]
  size: [130, 90]
  color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  inputs:
  - const_black
- name: null_cam
  type: nullTOP
  position: [1200, -2000]
  inputs:
  - flip_cam
- name: null_img
  type: nullTOP
  position: [1600, -2800]
  inputs:
  - blur_img
- name: spectrum
  type: audiospectrumCHOP
  parameters:
    fftsize: =parent.Ferro.par.Fftsize.menuIndex + 4
    frequencylog: =parent.Ferro.par.Logscale
    highfreqboost: 0
    outputmenu: setmanually
    outlength: 256
    autoexportroot: =parent()
  position: [400, 0]
  size: [130, 90]
  color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  inputs:
  - null_audio
- name: blur_sono
  type: blurTOP
  parameters:
    size: 12
  position: [2400, 0]
  inputs:
  - null_sono
- name: glsl_sono
  type: glslTOP
  parameters:
    pixeldat: glsl_sono_pixel
    outputresolution: custom
    format: rgba16float
  sequences:
    vec:
    - name: uSono
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Scrollspeed * absTime.frame // 1 - parent.Ferro.par.Scrollspeed * (absTime.frame - 1) // 1
      valuey: =parent.Ferro.par.Gain
      valuez: =parent.Ferro.par.Range
      valuew: =parent.Ferro.par.Tilt
    - name: uSmooth
      valuex: =1 - math.exp(-1.0 / (max(parent.Ferro.par.Attack, 0.001) * me.time.rate))
      valuey: =1 - math.exp(-1.0 / (max(parent.Ferro.par.Release, 0.001) * me.time.rate))
      valuez: =parent.Ferro.par.Specstart
      valuew: =parent.Ferro.par.Specend
    - name: uAgc
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Autogain
      valuey: =parent.Ferro.par.Recovery / me.time.rate
      valuez: =parent.Ferro.par.Silence
    - name: uSmooth2
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Freqsmooth
  position: [1600, 0]
  inputs:
  - feedback_sono
  - spectrum_tex
- name: lag_level
  type: lagCHOP
  parameters:
    lag1: 0.05
    lag2: 0.6
  position: [800, -1000]
  inputs:
  - analyze_rms
- name: null_sono
  type: nullTOP
  position: [2000, 0]
  inputs:
  - glsl_sono
- name: null_time
  type: nullCHOP
  position: [1200, -1200]
  inputs:
  - speed_time
- name: bloom_glow
  type: bloomTOP
  parameters:
    bloomthreshold: 0.85
    bloomintensity: =parent.Ferro.par.Bloom
  position: [4800, 0]
  size: [130, 90]
  color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  inputs:
  - glsl_shade
- name: blur_field
  type: blurTOP
  parameters:
    size: 10
  position: [2800, -2000]
  inputs:
  - null_state
- name: glsl_fluid
  type: glslmultiTOP
  parameters:
    pixeldat: glsl_fluid_pixel
    inputextenduv: hold
    premultrgbbyalpha: false
    outputresolution: custom
    resolutionw: 1280
    resolutionh: 720
    format: rgba16float
  sequences:
    color:
    - name: uBass
      rgbr: =parent.Ferro.par.Basscolorr
      rgbg: =parent.Ferro.par.Basscolorg
      rgbb: =parent.Ferro.par.Basscolorb
    - name: uLowmid
      rgbr: =parent.Ferro.par.Lowmidcolorr
      rgbg: =parent.Ferro.par.Lowmidcolorg
      rgbb: =parent.Ferro.par.Lowmidcolorb
    - name: uHighmid
      rgbr: =parent.Ferro.par.Highmidcolorr
      rgbg: =parent.Ferro.par.Highmidcolorg
      rgbb: =parent.Ferro.par.Highmidcolorb
    - name: uTreble
      rgbr: =parent.Ferro.par.Treblecolorr
      rgbg: =parent.Ferro.par.Treblecolorg
      rgbb: =parent.Ferro.par.Treblecolorb
    - name: uQuiet
      rgbr: =parent.Ferro.par.Quietcolorr
      rgbg: =parent.Ferro.par.Quietcolorg
      rgbb: =parent.Ferro.par.Quietcolorb
    - name: uPeak
      rgbr: =parent.Ferro.par.Peakcolorr
      rgbg: =parent.Ferro.par.Peakcolorg
      rgbb: =parent.Ferro.par.Peakcolorb
    vec:
    - name: uKal
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Kaleidomode.menuIndex
      valuey: =parent.Ferro.par.Segments
      valuez: =float(op('null_time')['spin']) * 2 * math.pi
      valuew: =parent.Ferro.par.Twist
    - name: uView
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Zoom * (1 + parent.Ferro.par.Zoompulse * min(1.0, float(op('null_level')[0]) * 10))
      valuey: =parent.Ferro.par.Gridcells
      valuez: =parent.Ferro.par.Gridshape.menuIndex
      valuew: =parent.Ferro.par.Gridamount
    - name: uSpike
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Idle
      valuey: =parent.Ferro.par.Wobble
      valuez: =parent.Ferro.par.Sharpness
      valuew: =parent.Ferro.par.Spikewidth
    - name: uMotion
      valuex: =float(op('null_time')['flow'])
      valuey: =tdu.clamp(float(op('null_viewer')['mass']) / max(parent.Ferro.par.Proximityrange, 0.01), 0, 1) * parent.Ferro.par.Videoactive
      valuez: =op('null_viewer')['cx']
      valuew: =op('null_viewer')['cy']
    - name: uPull
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Pull * parent.Ferro.par.Videoactive
      valuey: =parent.Ferro.par.Lens * parent.Ferro.par.Videoactive
      valuez: =parent.Ferro.par.Follow * parent.Ferro.par.Videoactive
      valuew: =parent.Ferro.par.Proximityzoom * parent.Ferro.par.Videoactive
    - name: uAmp
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Colorcurve
      valuey: =parent.Ferro.par.Peakthreshold
      valuez: =parent.Ferro.par.Peakmix
      valuew: =me.width / me.height
    - name: uKal2
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Pinch
      valuey: =parent.Ferro.par.Rings
      valuez: =float(op('null_time')["ring"]) * 2 * math.pi
      valuew: =math.radians(parent.Ferro.par.Sway) * math.sin(2 * math.pi * float(op('null_time')["sway"]))
    - name: uKal3
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Centerx
      valuey: =parent.Ferro.par.Centery
      valuez: =parent.Ferro.par.Tilesize
      valuew: =parent.Ferro.par.Tileoffset
    - name: uFrac
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Iterations
      valuey: =parent.Ferro.par.Foldscale
      valuez: =math.radians(parent.Ferro.par.Foldangle)
      valuew: =parent.Ferro.par.Foldoffset
    - name: uShape
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Spikeshape.menuIndex
      valuey: =parent.Ferro.par.Structure.menuIndex
      valuez: =parent.Ferro.par.Ridgewidth
      valuew: =math.radians(parent.Ferro.par.Gridrotate)
    - name: uShape2
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Cellrandom
      valuey: =parent.Ferro.par.Subgrid
      valuez: =parent.Ferro.par.Subgridscale
      valuew: =parent.Ferro.par.Tension
    - name: uShape3
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Height
      valuey: =min(parent.Ferro.par.Viscosity, 0.95)
      valuez: =parent.Ferro.par.Ripples
      valuew: =parent.Ferro.par.Ripplefreq
    - name: uWarp
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Warptype.menuIndex
      valuey: =parent.Ferro.par.Warpscale
      valuez: =parent.Ferro.par.Warpdetail
      valuew: =math.radians(parent.Ferro.par.Swirl)
    - name: uWarp2
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Swirlradius
    - name: uSono
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Bands
      valuey: =parent.Ferro.par.Freqlayout.menuIndex
      valuez: =parent.Ferro.par.Timeflow.menuIndex
      valuew: =parent.Ferro.par.Sonogamma
    - name: uSono2
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Onsetboost
      valuey: =min(1.0, float(op('null_level')[0]) * 10)
    - name: uImg
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Imgvisible * parent.Ferro.par.Videoactive
      valuey: =parent.Ferro.par.Imgrelief * parent.Ferro.par.Videoactive
      valuez: =parent.Ferro.par.Imgspikes * parent.Ferro.par.Videoactive
      valuew: =parent.Ferro.par.Imgsource.menuIndex
    - name: uImg2
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Imgcontrast
      valuey: =parent.Ferro.par.Imginvert
      valuez: =parent.Ferro.par.Imgkaleido
      valuew: =parent.Ferro.par.Imggain
  position: [4000, 0]
  size: [130, 90]
  color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  inputs:
  - null_sono
  - null_field
  - blur_sono
  - null_img
  - feedback_fluid
- name: glsl_shade
  type: glslTOP
  parameters:
    pixeldat: glsl_shade_pixel
    inputextenduv: hold
    format: rgba16float
  sequences:
    color:
    - name: uKey
      rgbr: =parent.Ferro.par.Keycolorr
      rgbg: =parent.Ferro.par.Keycolorg
      rgbb: =parent.Ferro.par.Keycolorb
    vec:
    - name: uLook
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Relief
      valuey: =parent.Ferro.par.Gloss
      valuez: =parent.Ferro.par.Reflection
      valuew: =parent.Ferro.par.Bodycolor
    - name: uLight
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Glow
      valuey: =parent.Ferro.par.Keylight
      valuez: =parent.Ferro.par.Rim
      valuew: =op('glsl_fluid').width / max(parent.Ferro.par.Gridcells, 1)
    - name: uView
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Debugview.menuIndex
      valuey: =op('null_viewer')['cx']
      valuez: =op('null_viewer')['cy']
      valuew: =parent.Ferro.par.Lightfollow * parent.Ferro.par.Videoactive * tdu.clamp(float(op('null_viewer')['mass']) * 20, 0, 1)
    - name: uExtra
      valuex: =parent.Ferro.par.Sonoglow
  position: [4400, 0]
  inputs:
  - glsl_fluid
  - null_field
  - null_sono
- name: lag_viewer
  type: lagCHOP
  parameters:
    lag1: 0.3
    lag2: 0.9
  position: [4400, -2000]
  inputs:
  - topto_viewer
- name: null_audio
  type: nullCHOP
  position: [-800, 0]
  inputs:
  - source: source_deck
    out: 1
- name: null_field
  type: nullTOP
  position: [3200, -2000]
  inputs:
  - blur_field
- name: null_final
  type: nullTOP
  position: [6000, 0]
  inputs:
  - CRT
- name: null_level
  type: nullCHOP
  position: [1200, -1000]
  inputs:
  - lag_level
- name: null_state
  type: nullTOP
  position: [2400, -2000]
  inputs:
  - glsl_presence
- name: null_video
  type: nullTOP
  position: [-800, -2000]
  inputs:
  - source_deck
- name: speed_time
  type: speedCHOP
  parameters:
    limittype: zigzag
    max: 1000
    autoexportroot: =parent()
  position: [800, -1200]
  size: [130, 90]
  color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  inputs:
  - const_rates
- name: window_out
  type: windowCOMP
  parameters:
    winop: null_final
    title: FerroScope
    size: custom
    winw: 1280
    winh: 720
  position: [6400, -400]
  size: [160, 130]
  color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
- name: analyze_rms
  type: analyzeCHOP
  parameters:
    function: rmspower
    autoexportroot: =parent()
  position: [400, -1000]
  size: [130, 90]
  color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  inputs:
  - null_audio
- name: const_black
  type: constantTOP
  parameters:
    colorr: 0
    colorg: 0
    colorb: 0
    resolutionw: 160
    resolutionh: 90
  position: [-2000, -2400]
- name: const_rates
  type: constantCHOP
  sequences:
    const:
    - name: flow
      value: =parent.Ferro.par.Flowspeed * (1 + parent.Ferro.par.Agitation * min(1.0, float(op('null_level')[0]) * 10))
    - name: spin
      value: =parent.Ferro.par.Spin / 360.0 * (1 + parent.Ferro.par.Spinreact * min(1.0, float(op('null_level')[0]) * 10))
    - name: sway
      value: =parent.Ferro.par.Swayspeed
    - name: ring
      value: =parent.Ferro.par.Ringspin / 360.0
  position: [400, -1200]
- name: glsl_viewer
  type: glslTOP
  parameters:
    pixeldat: glsl_viewer_pixel
    outputresolution: custom
    resolutionw: 1
    resolutionh: 1
    format: rgba32float
  position: [3600, -2000]
  inputs:
  - null_field
- name: null_viewer
  type: nullCHOP
  position: [4800, -2000]
  inputs:
  - lag_viewer
- name: tonemap_out
  type: tonemapTOP
  parameters:
    exposurebias: =parent.Ferro.par.Exposure
    format: rgba8fixed
  position: [5200, 0]
  size: [130, 90]
  color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  inputs:
  - bloom_glow
- name: spectrum_tex
  type: choptoTOP
  parameters:
    chop: spectrum
    format: mono32float
  position: [800, 0]
  size: [130, 90]
  color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
- name: topto_viewer
  type: toptoCHOP
  parameters:
    top: glsl_viewer
    r: cx
    g: cy
    b: mass
    a: peak
    outputcolorspace: passthrough
    rate: =me.time.rate
    autoexportroot: =parent()
  position: [4000, -2000]
  size: [130, 90]
  color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
- name: const_silence
  type: constantCHOP
  sequences:
    const:
    - name: silence
  position: [-2000, 200]
- name: feedback_sono
  type: feedbackTOP
  parameters:
    top: null_sono
  position: [1200, -200]
  inputs:
  - const_sono_seed
- name: glsl_presence
  type: glslTOP
  parameters:
    pixeldat: glsl_presence_pixel
    format: rgba16float
  sequences:
    vec:
    - name: uPres
      valuex: =0.30 - 0.25 * parent.Ferro.par.Sensitivity
      valuey: =parent.Ferro.par.Presenceweight
      valuez: =parent.Ferro.par.Motionweight
      valuew: =0.12 - 0.09 * parent.Ferro.par.Sensitivity
    - name: uRates
      valuex: 0.35
      valuey: 0.02
      valuez: 0.03
      valuew: 0.0005
  position: [2000, -2000]
  inputs:
  - null_cam
  - feedback_state
  - feedback_prevcam
- name: feedback_fluid
  type: feedbackTOP
  parameters:
    top: glsl_fluid
  position: [3600, -400]
  inputs:
  - const_fluid_seed
- name: feedback_state
  type: feedbackTOP
  parameters:
    top: null_state
  position: [1600, -2200]
  inputs:
  - const_state_seed
- name: glsl_sono_info
  type: infoDAT
  parameters:
    op: glsl_sono
  position: [1675, -120]
  dock: glsl_sono
  dat_read_only: true
- name: const_sono_seed
  type: constantTOP
  parameters:
    colorr: 0
    colorg: 0
    colorb: 0
    alpha: 0
    format: rgba16float
  position: [800, -200]
- name: glsl_fluid_info
  type: infoDAT
  parameters:
    op: glsl_fluid
  position: [4075, -120]
  dock: glsl_fluid
  dat_read_only: true
- name: glsl_shade_info
  type: infoDAT
  parameters:
    op: glsl_shade
  position: [4475, -120]
  dock: glsl_shade
  dat_read_only: true
- name: glsl_sono_pixel
  type: textDAT
  parameters:
    file: project1/ferroscope/glsl_sono_pixel.glsl
  position: [1525, -120]
  dock: glsl_sono
- name: const_fluid_seed
  type: constantTOP
  parameters:
    colorr: 0
    colorg: 0
    colorb: 0
    alpha: 0
    resolutionw: 1280
    resolutionh: 720
    format: rgba16float
  position: [3200, -400]
- name: const_state_seed
  type: constantTOP
  parameters:
    colorr: -1
    colorg: -1
    colorb: -1
    alpha: 0
    resolutionw: 160
    resolutionh: 90
    format: rgba16float
  position: [1200, -2200]
- name: feedback_prevcam
  type: feedbackTOP
  parameters:
    top: null_cam
  position: [1600, -2400]
  inputs:
  - null_cam
- name: glsl_fluid_pixel
  type: textDAT
  parameters:
    file: project1/ferroscope/glsl_fluid_pixel.glsl
  position: [3925, -120]
  dock: glsl_fluid
- name: glsl_shade_pixel
  type: textDAT
  parameters:
    file: project1/ferroscope/glsl_shade_pixel.glsl
  position: [4325, -120]
  dock: glsl_shade
- name: glsl_viewer_info
  type: infoDAT
  parameters:
    op: glsl_viewer
  position: [3675, -2120]
  dock: glsl_viewer
  dat_read_only: true
- name: glsl_viewer_pixel
  type: textDAT
  parameters:
    file: project1/ferroscope/glsl_viewer_pixel.glsl
  position: [3525, -2120]
  dock: glsl_viewer
- name: controls_callbacks
  type: parameterexecuteDAT
  parameters:
    fromop: =parent()
    op: ..
    pars: Resetsono Relearnbg Openwindow Closewindow Videorestart Audiorestart Videodownload Audiodownload Applypreset Storepreset
    valuechange: false
    builtin: false
    file: project1/ferroscope/controls_callbacks.py
    syncfile: true
  position: [6000, -400]
  size: [130, 90]
  color: [0.9, 0.3, 0.4]
  tags:
  - py
- name: glsl_presence_info
  type: infoDAT
  parameters:
    op: glsl_presence
  position: [2075, -2120]
  dock: glsl_presence
  dat_read_only: true
- name: glsl_presence_pixel
  type: textDAT
  parameters:
    file: project1/ferroscope/glsl_presence_pixel.glsl
  position: [1925, -2120]
  dock: glsl_presence
annotations:
- name: annotate1
  mode: annotate
  title: Audio Source -> Sonogram
  text: 'Audio comes from source_deck (Audio Source on the Sources page: microphone, audio file, the external audio input (FerroScope''s 2nd connector, passed through in_audio; silence from const_silence when nothing is wired), or YouTube audio) -> null_audio; source_deck also plays it to the speakers. null_audio -> spectrum (FFT, log bins) -> spectrum_tex. glsl_sono writes the newest spectrum on the top row and scrolls older rows down (feedback via null_sono): R = loudness after Auto Gain, attack and release; G = onset; B = tracked peak. blur_sono feeds the smooth pool.'
  position: [-2070, -270]
  size: [4670, 930]
  color: [0.2, 0.35, 0.45]
  opacity: 0.6
- name: annotate2
  mode: annotate
  title: Clocks and Loudness
  text: analyze_rms -> lag_level = overall loudness, which speeds the liquid (Sound Agitation). const_rates -> speed_time integrates liquid speed and kaleidoscope spin into smooth clocks (null_time).
  position: [330, -1270]
  size: [1070, 530]
  color: [0.3, 0.32, 0.3]
  opacity: 0.6
- name: annotate3
  mode: annotate
  title: Video Source -> Viewer Field
  text: 'Video comes from source_deck (Video Source on the Sources page: webcam, movie file, the external video input (FerroScope''s 1st connector, passed through in_video; black from const_black when nothing is wired), or YouTube video) -> null_video. At 160x90, mirrored: glsl_presence learns the empty room (feedback via null_state) and marks the viewer by difference from the room plus motion; blur_field -> null_field is the magnet field. glsl_viewer reduces it to centre + coverage -> null_viewer. Bottom row: the picture at 640x360 (fit_img -> flip_img -> blur_img -> null_img) for the Image page.'
  position: [-2070, -2870]
  size: [7070, 1130]
  color: [0.35, 0.25, 0.45]
  opacity: 0.6
- name: annotate4
  mode: annotate
  title: Ferrofluid Render and Output
  text: 'glsl_fluid (GLSL Multi): hex or square spike lattice with honeycomb ridges and a nested sub-grid; heights and colours from the kaleidoscope-folded sonogram (8 modes); liquid warp and swirl; raised, leaned and lensed toward the viewer; camera picture as colour, relief or spikes; feedback_fluid feeds back the last frame for viscosity. glsl_shade: black glossy body, white key highlight, sound-coloured rim, tip glow, sonogram glow. bloom -> ACES tone map -> CRT (reusable filter) -> out1; window_out shows null_final in its own window; controls_callbacks handles the pulse buttons and forwards the source and transport ones to source_deck.'
  position: [3130, -670]
  size: [3500, 970]
  color: [0.45, 0.3, 0.2]
  opacity: 0.6
- name: annotate5
  mode: annotate
  title: Source Deck (shared module)
  text: 'source_deck is the shared sources-and-transport module, loaded from ../00-custom-modules/source-deck/source_deck.tox (External .tox, Reload Custom Parameters off, so its settings stay in this project). Its parameters are bound to FerroScope''s Sources and Transport pages plus Camera On and Microphone On, so this panel drives it; controls_callbacks forwards the Restart and Download pulses. It is tagged tdxn_exclude: the module''s own text lives beside its .tox. Video out -> null_video, audio out -> null_audio.'
  position: [-1670, -1070]
  size: [1270, 400]
  color: [0.2, 0.4, 0.3]
  opacity: 0.6
